<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barkur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barkur is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udupi">Udupi</a> district of coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, once a major town and the later capital of the Alupa dynasty. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> it was the seat of a province governing the Tulu country. Ruined temples, Jain shrines and fort remains survive from its medieval prosperity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/barkur.jpg" alt="Barkur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudolph.A.furtado · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barkur_main_town..JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
